          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "k8ejI",
              "name": "Section title",
              "fill": "$foreground",
              "content": "v2/Badge",
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "iZR48",
              "name": "Section note",
              "fill": "$muted-foreground",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 900,
              "content": "One badge, six looks, set by root fill and Label fill. Neutral (muted, ink-2): file quality, Manual download, 2 versions. Strong (black, white): In library, stays visible on a selected row. Lime (best, black text): best release and Downloading 64%, with Dot on. Risk (risk-soft, risk): Hit and run risk, Stalled, Failed. Warning (warning-soft, warning): Missing 2 episodes, Below cutoff. Outline (1 px line-strong, ink-2): Not out yet, Searching with Spinner on. Not interactive, so no hover or focus. Maps to shadcn Badge variants secondary, default, best (custom), destructive, warning (custom), outline. Icon: optional 12 px lucide icon before the label, off by default; turn it on and set its icon for states such as Not monitored (bookmark-x). Spinner stays for Searching only. Size: 20 px high (badge-h), badge-px 6, badge-text 11, 12 px icons (badge-icon). Plain: no fill and no padding, a 14 px foreground check and muted words at 13 px, 28 px high, built from the row tokens (control-h-row, control-text-row, control-icon-row) so it lines up with the row button beside it. Use plain for a standing status next to a row button, such as In library on a search result. A filled badge never takes button height, or it reads as a button.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            },
